        explanation:
          "Now, turn to how social media interacts with Sweden's own established broadcast political-debate tradition. SVT's periodic party-leader debates, alongside the flagship Agenda program covered earlier in this lecture, remain central set-piece moments in the Swedish political-communication calendar, but social media, increasingly used by Swedish party leaders and officials for direct-to-public communication, has introduced a parallel layer of real-time commentary, clipping, and reaction that now runs simultaneously alongside these televised debates, with specific exchanges frequently clipped and recirculated on social platforms within minutes, reaching audiences well beyond the broadcast's own live viewership and often outlasting the broadcast's own initial framing in public memory.",
